      "side": 1,
      "message": "The subject says \"global byte unit\", but `VM_COMMIT_SHIFT` is `PAGE_SHIFT_4KB`, so the counter counts 4KB units. Could the subject say that, e.g. \"ANDROID: P3S: mm: Account commitments in 4KB units\"?\n\nCould the body also say what fails without the patch? As far as I can see, each charge and its uncharge already use the same unit today. The VMA paths count pages of the mm (their files include `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`, and `exit_mmap()` and `create_init_stack_vma()` run under `P3S_CONTEXT_REMOTE_MM()`), and shmem and swapoff count kernel pages. What goes wrong is the shared counter and its limits:\n\n- `Committed_AS` shows a 4KB process\u0027s commitments four times over.\n- Under the default `OVERCOMMIT_GUESS` policy, one accounted mmap of a 4KB process can\u0027t exceed a quarter of RAM plus swap, because `pages \u003e totalram_pages() + total_swap_pages` compares 4KB pages with kernel pages.\n- Strict overcommit counts a 4KB process\u0027s commitments four times against the limit.\n\nI think the imbalance on fragmented unmaps, mremap and mprotect would only appear with a kernel-page counter, so it reads best as the reason for picking 4KB units. Also, \"Add accounting and strict-overcommit checks.\" doesn\u0027t match the code, which converts the existing checks, and the tests are in aosp/4367986. Would it be OK to drop that sentence?",
      "isAi": true,
