      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would you mind moving the new wrappers out of `\u003clinux/mman.h\u003e`? `vm_acct_memory_units()`, `vm_acct_memory_mm()` and `vm_unacct_memory_mm()` could live in a new `include/linux/p3s/mman.h` that `\u003clinux/mman.h\u003e` includes once at the end, together with `vm_memory_committed_kbytes()` as a `static inline`. Upstream\u0027s part of the header would then only change inside `vm_acct_memory()`:\n\n```\nstatic inline void vm_acct_memory(long pages)\n{\n\tpercpu_counter_add_batch(\u0026vm_committed_as, vm_commit_native_pages(pages),\n\t\t\t\t vm_committed_as_batch);\n}\n```\n\nWith the conversion helpers in `include/linux/p3s/mm.h`, the wrappers fold to upstream\u0027s code without `CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE`, so the new header wouldn\u0027t need a config block.",
