      "writtenOn": "2026-11-01T04:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried this breaks `!CONFIG_SECURITY` builds. `vm_commit_mm_pages()` and `vm_commit_native_pages()` are only declared in `\u003clinux/mman.h\u003e`, which neither `\u003clinux/security.h\u003e` nor `\u003clinux/mm.h\u003e` includes on arm64. A local build with `CONFIG_SECURITY` disabled fails in these two stubs with \"call to undeclared function\", and `arch/arm64/configs/crashdump_defconfig` (the `kernel_aarch64_crashdump` target) doesn\u0027t enable `CONFIG_SECURITY`.\n\nWith the helpers as `static inline` in `include/linux/p3s/mm.h` (see my comment on `mm/util.c`), `\u003clinux/mm.h\u003e` already reaches them through `\u003clinux/mm_types.h\u003e`, so the stubs would build again.",
