      "writtenOn": "2026-11-01T04:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it be OK to keep `vm_commit_limit()` as upstream wrote it, and convert once in `__vm_enough_memory()`? Only the `overcommit_kbytes` conversion would change, to `PAGE_SHIFT_KERNEL`, because `mm/util.c` is opted in and `PAGE_SHIFT` there is the caller\u0027s page size. Then:\n\n```\n\tallowed \u003d vm_commit_native_pages(vm_commit_limit());\n```\n\nThat drops `vm_commit_limit_units()`, `native_scale` and the `DIV_ROUND_UP()` wrapper, and `CommitLimit` keeps upstream\u0027s value (today it rounds `overcommit_kbytes` up instead of down). The strict limit would lose less than one kernel page of `overcommit_kbytes`, as it does upstream on 16KB kernels.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "f79c7e87fd32f53fac257c9e41d0356074b9a82d",
