      "writtenOn": "2026-11-01T04:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would you mind moving `VM_COMMIT_SHIFT`, `vm_commit_native_pages()` and `vm_commit_mm_pages()` into `include/linux/p3s/mm.h`, next to `mm_kernel_pages()` (aosp/4368094)? The constant can go into its existing `#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE` block, and the helpers after the block, since `mm_pte_shift()` already has a stub:\n\n```\n/* in the CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE block */\n#define VM_COMMIT_SHIFT\t\tPAGE_SHIFT_4KB\n/* in its #else branch */\n#define VM_COMMIT_SHIFT\t\tPAGE_SHIFT_KERNEL\n\n/* after the block, next to mm_kernel_pages() */\nstatic inline long vm_commit_mm_pages(const struct mm_struct *mm, long pages)\n{\n\treturn pages * (1L \u003c\u003c (mm_pte_shift(mm) - VM_COMMIT_SHIFT));\n}\n\nstatic inline long vm_commit_native_pages(long pages)\n{\n\treturn pages * (1L \u003c\u003c (PAGE_SHIFT_KERNEL - VM_COMMIT_SHIFT));\n}\n```\n\nThat removes all three `#ifdef` blocks from `mm/util.c` and the prototypes from `\u003clinux/mman.h\u003e`.\n\nIt also matters for native builds. Because the helpers are out of line, the inline `vm_acct_memory()` and `vm_unacct_memory_mm()`, and `security_vm_enough_memory_mm()`, now make a function call on every accounted mmap, munmap, mprotect and brk. That includes x86_64 and builds without `CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE`. As `static inline` helpers, they fold back to upstream\u0027s code there.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "f79c7e87fd32f53fac257c9e41d0356074b9a82d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
